/-!
# the coordinate sections of `φ^*𝒪(1)` and their divisors

Source: `rmk:bdiv:L749` (GAGA for divisors on the algebraized models).

For a morphism `φ : V → ℙʳ` over `ℂ` whose complex points are `φ(z) = [u₀(z) : ⋯ : u_r(z)]`
near a point (`u` holomorphic without common zero), the analytic divisor ideal of the pulled-back
coordinate section `φ^*y_k` of the algebraic line bundle `φ^*𝒪(1)` (Codex's
`originalMapHyperplaneBundle`) is generated by `u_k` (`coordSection_ideal_mem`): in the frame
`φ^*y_i` (`u_i ≠ 0`) its coefficient is `φ^*(y_k/y_i)`, whose analytic function is `u_k/u_i`.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false

noncomputable section

namespace SGPT.BDivisor.BD6

